hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"138801","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi' from Abdullah ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Whoever purchases food, let him not sell it until he takes possession of it."""
"138802","Yahya related to me from Malik that it reached him that Umar ibn al-Khattab spoke about a man who gave a salam (advance payment) to another man for food on condition that he give it to him in another land. Umar ibn al-Khattab disliked that and said: ""Where is the transport?"" meaning the cost of transporting it."
"138901","[1389] Malik told me that he had heard that a man came to Abdullah bin Omar and said: O Abu Abdul Rahman, I have asked A man who is a predecessor, and I made a better condition for him than what I made. Abdullah bin Omar said: That is usury. He said: How do you command me, O Abu Abdul Rahman? Abdullah said: Advances are based on three aspects: a predecessor is a predecessor seeking the face of God, so you have the face of God, and a predecessor is a predecessor you seek. If you want the honor of your companion, you will have the honor of your companion, and an advance you will give in order to take what is evil for what is good. That is usury. He said: How do you command me, O Abu Abdul Rahman? He said: I think that you should tear the paper in pieces, and if he gives you the same as what you borrowed, you accept it, and if he gives you less than what you borrowed. So you take him and you will be rewarded, and if he gives you better than what you asked him for and is good to himself, then that is his gratitude to you, and to you The reward for what you have seen.\\nMota in front of Malik Hadith: 1389 Arabic Hadith:"
"138902","[1389] Malik told me that he had heard that a man came to Abdullah bin Omar and said: O Abu Abdul Rahman, I have asked A man who is a predecessor, and I made a better condition for him than what I made. Abdullah bin Omar said: That is usury. He said: How do you command me, O Abu Abdul Rahman? Abdullah said: Advances are based on three aspects: a predecessor is a predecessor seeking the face of God, so you have the face of God, and a predecessor is a predecessor you seek. If you want the honor of your companion, you will have the honor of your companion, and an advance you will give in order to take what is evil for what is good. That is usury. He said: How do you command me, O Abu Abdul Rahman? He said: I think that you should tear the paper in pieces, and if he gives you the same as what you borrowed, you accept it, and if he gives you less than what you borrowed. So you take him and you will be rewarded, and if he gives you better than what you asked him for and is good to himself, then that is his gratitude to you, and to you The reward for what you have seen.\\nMota in front of Malik Hadith: 1389 Arabic Hadith:"
